## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical mastery of multi-layer caching, invalidation patterns, and race-condition handling under high load. It probes Redis and Memcached integration, Lua-based locks, and cross-region TTL coherence.

## Key Concepts
- Cache invalidation strategies across layers
- Redis pub/sub and keyspace notifications
- Per-key mutex with Lua scripting to prevent stampedes
- Write-through vs write-behind coherence
- Multi-region TTL synchronization

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: acquire per-key lock, fetch fresh data, set both caches
function getFeed(key) {
  if (Redis.get(key)) return Redis.get(key)
  if (Memcache.add(key + ':lock', 1, 1)) {
    const fresh = loadFromDB(key)
    Redis.set(key, fresh, 300)
    Memcache.set(key, fresh, 300)
    Memcache.delete(key + ':lock')
    return fresh
  } else {
    // wait and retry
  }
}
```

